WMMA 4-bit GEMM tuning overrides (not part of the bitsandbytes PR).

Adds a -DBNB_WMMA_DEV=ON CMake option (off by default). When on, the build reads these
environment variables on every 4-bit GEMM call:
  BNB_GEMM4BIT_KERNEL=simt|wmma         force the SIMT or WMMA kernel (bench.py)
  BNB_WMMA_CFG=wm,wn,warps_m,warps_n,ksplit,kch   force one WMMA tile from wmma_dev_shapes (sweep.py)
  BNB_WMMA_ROW_TILES_FIRST=0|1          override the block order
  BNB_WMMA_PRESCALE=0|1                 override the gfx11 fp16 B pre-scaling

Apply from the repository root on top of the WMMA kernel (git apply <this file>), then build with
-DBNB_WMMA_DEV=ON. The benchmark/rocm-wmma-gemm-4bit branch already has it applied.

